  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#rel-icon\n\n> Link type \"icon\"\n\nSome sites use a `canvas` and then update the `<link rel=icon>`'s `href` to the `canvas`'s `toDataURL()`, e.g. to implement an animated icon or to show how many unread messages there are.\n\nI discussed with @fsoder in the context of [supporting SVG favicons in Chromium](https://code.google.com/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=294179) and it seems like it would be better to be able to link to an in-document `svg` or `canvas` element directly for those use cases. Round-tripping via a data: URL is basically unnecessary overhead in principle.\n",
